STEP 1: Open Rainmeter folder in your File Explorer
STEP 2: Open Skins folder 
STEP 3: Create A New Folder named Rolling30DayCalendar
STEP 4: Download this ZIP  
STEP 5: Copy @Resourses Folder and MiniCalendar.ini File
STEP 5: Paste Them in the Folder created in Skins folder
STEP 7: Open Rainmeter from taskbar where this icon is there  " ^ "
STEP 8: Click Refresh and then Double Click the MiniCalendar.ini file to get this Skin in your Desktop


The Mini Calendar.png looks Purple but it depends on your Desktop Background as the Calender is Translucent

